== (a) actual realizable set of q+2 random columns (rank q): 2-dim subgroup inside R(X)?
  q=4: 28/30 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^6/3^q density)
  q=5: 26/30 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^7/3^q density)
  q=6: 19/30 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^8/3^q density)
  q=7: 22/30 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^9/3^q density)
  q=8: 16/30 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^10/3^q density)
  q=9: 5/10 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^11/3^q density)
  q=10: 3/10 instances have a 2-dim subgroup inside R(X) (|R| ~ 2^12/3^q density)
